{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.55,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U10", "U11"],
      "pins": ["U10.4", "U10.5", "U11.4", "U11.5"],
      "nets": ["GND", "5V_switched_CAN", "SERIAL_CAN_PWR_3.3V"],
      "observed": "Both isolated CAN transceivers U10 and U11 (CA-IS3050G / ISO1050DUB) have GND1 (pin 4) and GND2 (pin 5) tied to the single system GND net, and the bus-side supply 5V_switched_CAN is also decoupled to that same GND (C15/C16 pin 1 on GND). There is no separate isolated ground net anywhere in the netlist.",
      "expected": "For an isolated CAN transceiver the primary (MCU-side) ground GND1 and the secondary (bus-side) ground GND2 must be separate nets to provide galvanic isolation between the CM4 domain and the CAN bus, as the specification states the board implements 'two isolated CAN buses ... through an isolated CAN transceiver'.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (CAN0, CAN1), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller (U8, U9) through an isolated CAN transceiver (U11/companion)"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") ... ) (node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") ... ) (node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") ... ) (node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") ... )"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"52\") (name \"5V_switched_CAN\") (node (ref \"C15\") (pin \"1\") ...) (node (ref \"C16\") (pin \"1\") ...)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The galvanic isolation between the rover CAN bus and the CM4 compute/ground domain is defeated; the interface will not break ground loops or protect the MCU from bus-side transients as intended, behaving as a non-isolated CAN bus.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    },
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["R58", "U34", "U7", "Q10"],
      "pins": ["R58.1", "U34.2", "U34.4", "U7.5", "Q10.1"],
      "nets": ["/LED_3.3V_POWER_NONINV", "+3V3", "GND"],
      "observed": "The active-high enable node /LED_3.3V_POWER_NONINV is pulled to GND by R58 and is only driven by the open-drain output Y of U34 (SN74LVC1G07) whose input A (pin 2) is tied directly to +3V3. With A = VCC, U34's open-drain output can never sink, so /LED_3.3V_POWER_NONINV is permanently held low. This node drives U7 (TXS0101) OE and Q10 gate (the WS2812 ground switch).",
      "expected": "Per the specification the board provides working addressable WS2812B status LEDs; the U7 level-shifter OE and the Q10 WS2812 ground switch must be able to go high, so the enable net should be pull-up driven (or U34 should be a sinkable control), not stuck at GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U34\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") ...)"} on +3V3, "(node (ref \"U34\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"Y\") ...)" on /LED_3.3V_POWER_NONINV, "(node (ref \"R58\") (pin \"1\") ...) on GND", "(node (ref \"U7\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"OE\") ...) on /LED_3.3V_POWER_NONINV"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Addressable status LEDs (WS2812B, D5-D7, D18-D21)"}
      ],
      "impact": "U7 (the 3.3V->5V WS2812 data level shifter) and Q10 (WS2812 ground return) are permanently disabled, so the WS2812B status LEDs cannot light regardless of the GPIO13 data or the /LED_EN DIP switch.",
      "confidence": 0.35
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows the isolated CAN transceivers U10/U11 with GND1 and GND2 both tied to the single system GND (and the bus-side rail decoupled to GND), defeating the galvanic isolation the specification states for CAN0/CAN1; a second, lower-confidence issue is the WS2812 enable net /LED_3.3V_POWER_NONINV being permanently held low, which would disable the addressable status LEDs."
}

